but a buyer who is shopping with

279
00:11:34,148 --> 00:11:36,723
a calculator will usually end up on

280
00:11:36,723 --> 00:11:38,047
the Maverick side.

281
00:11:38,396 --> 00:11:40,308
There is also a question of what

282
00:11:40,308 --> 00:11:41,682
a buyer wants to carry.

283
00:11:41,862 --> 00:11:44,290
The Santa Cruz bed is four feet

284
00:11:44,290 --> 00:11:47,344
long and holds twenty-seven cubic feet,

285
00:11:47,344 --> 00:11:49,849
and the Maverick bed is four and

286
00:11:49,849 --> 00:11:51,181
a half feet long,

287
00:11:51,181 --> 00:11:53,217
according to The Autopian.

288
00:11:53,397 --> 00:11:56,235
That half foot matters for things like

289
00:11:56,235 --> 00:11:57,431
a mountain bike,

290
00:11:57,431 --> 00:11:58,925
a few bags of mulch,

291
00:11:58,925 --> 00:12:00,792
or two sheets of plywood.

292
00:12:00,972 --> 00:12:03,176
If your hauling is occasional,

293
00:12:03,176 --> 00:12:04,571
either truck works.

294
00:12:04,751 --> 00:12:06,398
If it is every week,

295
00:12:06,398 --> 00:12:09,610
the bed will decide the purchase before

296
00:12:09,610 --> 00:12:10,928
the engine does.

297
00:12:11,277 --> 00:12:13,406
Now think about what happens to the

298
00:12:13,406 --> 00:12:15,169
owner of a truck that may not

299
00:12:15,169 --> 00:12:16,142
get a successor.

300
00:12:16,322 --> 00:12:18,268
The warranty stays in place,

301
00:12:18,268 --> 00:12:20,979
and Hyundai has to keep supplying parts

302
00:12:20,979 --> 00:12:21,674
for years.

303
00:12:21,854 --> 00:12:24,014
That part is not a real risk.

304
00:12:24,194 --> 00:12:26,701
The real risk is resale.

305
00:12:26,881 --> 00:12:29,748
If buyers believe a model is ending,

306
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:31,978
used prices can fall faster.

307
00:12:32,158 --> 00:12:34,186
We do not have a resale figure

308
00:12:34,186 --> 00:12:36,484
for the Santa Cruz in our sources,

309
00:12:36,484 --> 00:12:38,242
so we will not invent one.

310
00:12:38,422 --> 00:12:40,082
But it is fair to say that

311
00:12:40,082 --> 00:12:42,253
this is the number a careful buyer

312
00:12:42,253 --> 00:12:44,041
should ask the dealer about.

313
00:12:44,391 --> 00:12:46,888
And what about the twenty twenty-seven price?

314
00:12:47,068 --> 00:12:49,639
Kelley Blue Book lists the range as

315
00:12:49,639 --> 00:12:53,533
thirty-one thousand, nine hundred fifty to forty-four

316
00:12:53,533 --> 00:12:56,692
thousand, four hundred twenty-five dollars.

317
00:12:56,872 --> 00:12:58,912
At the same time it shows a

318
00:12:58,912 --> 00:13:01,026
deal ending November second,

319
00:13:01,026 --> 00:13:03,896
so dealers are willing to move trucks.

320
00:13:04,076 --> 00:13:06,081
A buyer who is patient,

321
00:13:06,081 --> 00:13:08,782
and who has a Maverick quote in

322
00:13:08,782 --> 00:13:11,309
hand, can use it as leverage.

323
00:13:11,489 --> 00:13:13,472
The best time to negotiate on a

324
00:13:13,472 --> 00:13:15,839
model with high inventory is when the

325
00:13:15,839 --> 00:13:18,142
dealer has had the truck for months.

326
00:13:18,491 --> 00:13:21,533
Finally, a note about reading headlines.

327
00:13:21,713 --> 00:13:24,054
The first report said the Santa Cruz

328
00:13:24,054 --> 00:13:24,639
was dead.

329
00:13:24,819 --> 00:13:26,801
Hyundai did not confirm it,

330
00:13:26,801 --> 00:13:29,370
and then it confirmed the opposite,

331
00:13:29,370 --> 00:13:31,204
that the truck continues.

332
00:13:31,384 --> 00:13:32,564
Both can be true,

333
00:13:32,564 --> 00:13:34,923
because a model can continue for a

334
00:13:34,923 --> 00:13:37,073
year and still be near the end.

335
00:13:37,253 --> 00:13:40,511
Companies rarely announce an ending far in

336
00:13:40,511 --> 00:13:41,131
advance.

337
00:13:41,311 --> 00:13:43,731
So treat a continuing model as a

338
00:13:43,731 --> 00:13:46,075
truck with an uncertain future,

339
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:49,554
and decide whether that uncertainty matters to

340
00:13:49,554 --> 00:13:49,856
you.

341
00:13:50,205 --> 00:13:52,702
Part four, what comes next.

342
00:13:52,882 --> 00:13:56,942
Hyundai confirmed a new midsize body-on-frame pickup

343
00:13:56,942 --> 00:14:00,300
at its twenty twenty-five CEO Investor Day.

344
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:02,574
The company says it will reach the

345
00:14:02,574 --> 00:14:04,730
United States before twenty thirty.

346
00:14:04,910 --> 00:14:07,708
Automotive News reports twenty twenty-nine.

347
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:10,619
The Autopian expects it to be bigger

348
00:14:10,619 --> 00:14:12,136
than the Santa Cruz,

349
00:14:12,136 --> 00:14:14,868
and to compete with the Ford Ranger,

350
00:14:14,868 --> 00:14:16,613
the Chevrolet Colorado,

351
00:14:16,613 --> 00:14:19,800
the Toyota Tacoma and the Honda Ridgeline.

352
00:14:20,149 --> 00:14:22,738
That tells us what the Santa Cruz

353
00:14:22,738 --> 00:14:23,052
was.

354
00:14:23,232 --> 00:14:24,973
It was Hyundai's test.

355
00:14:25,153 --> 00:14:27,810
The company called it a new type

356
00:14:27,810 --> 00:14:31,047
